WEBVTT

00:00:00.015 --> 00:00:03.309
Easy Science. How Do Bees Make Honey?

00:00:03.309 --> 00:00:07.665
Honey is made by bees, and it takes a great deal of work.

00:00:07.665 --> 00:00:09.550
It begins with flowers.

00:00:09.550 --> 00:00:12.648
Inside many flowers there is a sweet water.

00:00:12.648 --> 00:00:16.005
A bee flies from flower to flower and drinks it.

00:00:16.005 --> 00:00:17.815
She does not eat it all.

00:00:17.815 --> 00:00:21.156
She keeps most of it in a special second stomach.

00:00:21.156 --> 00:00:24.531
When this stomach is full, she flies home.

00:00:24.531 --> 00:00:28.096
A bee may visit a thousand flowers to fill it once.

00:00:28.096 --> 00:00:31.468
At home she gives the sweet water to other bees.

00:00:31.468 --> 00:00:33.802
They pass it from mouth to mouth.

00:00:33.802 --> 00:00:36.864
As they do this, it slowly changes.

00:00:36.864 --> 00:00:42.018
Then the bees put it into small rooms with six sides, made of wax.

00:00:42.018 --> 00:00:44.644
But it still has too much water in it.

00:00:44.644 --> 00:00:49.283
So the bees move their wings very fast, like little fans.

00:00:49.283 --> 00:00:52.676
The moving air dries it, and it becomes thick.

00:00:52.676 --> 00:00:54.016
Now it is honey.

00:00:54.016 --> 00:00:57.317
The bees close each small room with more wax.

00:00:57.317 --> 00:01:01.359
This is their food for the winter, when there are no flowers.

00:01:01.359 --> 00:01:07.602
One bee makes only a very small amount of honey in her whole life, less than a small spoon.

00:01:07.602 --> 00:01:11.541
A jar of honey is the work of many thousands of bees.
